            <ArticleTitle>Radiological erosions in frozen shoulder.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>293-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Erosions of the humeral head can occur in the frozen shoulder, with or without other radiological features. True erosions need to be distinguished from radiographic projectional artefacts. The presence of an erosion does not affect the prognosis adversely.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
